# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree, not just in the index.
#
# This is load-bearing for Phase 0 rather than tidiness. Two checks compare file
# *content*: the schema-immutability check compares a version file against the
# content at the commit that introduced it, read from git, and 3.8 asserts that
# re-running the extraction produces byte-identical output. On Windows the
# default `core.autocrlf` behaviour gives the working tree CRLF while git stores
# LF, so both comparisons would fail on a clean checkout for a reason that has
# nothing to do with schemas or the extraction. `eol=lf` makes the working tree
# byte-identical to what git stores, so "unchanged" means unchanged.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts, never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.lock binary
